{
  "abstract": "We apply QuIP's fourth-root preconditioner to diagonal output functional Fisher while preserving the rotated input Gram and its BlockLDLQ factors. Under assumptions A1–A2 on normalized noise and diagonal Kronecker-Fisher distortion, the restoration scale minimizes modeled loss. We select shrinkage without quantization and allocate four BW16 rates and FP16 scales across body and vocabulary matrices with a byte-constrained knapsack, exact for the scored surrogate.\n\nIn weight-only Qwen3-4B and Qwen3-8B experiments, matched-byte 2×2 controls show that mixed-domain input calibration and damping drive GSM8K gains, while Fisher allocation and scaling lower English Teacher-KL. On 8B at 2.25 bpw, Fisher allocation and scaling lower mixed-domain baseline Teacher-KL by 0.0275/0.0240 nats on WikiText-2/C4. GSM8K-Holdout-1024 moves from 87.89% to 86.82% (p = 0.334). Standard WikiText-2/C4 perplexity falls from 11.20/13.81 to 11.09/13.68 on that 8B contrast. On 4B it falls from 16.14/17.62 for uniform prose BW16 to 15.42/17.03 for the combined package. The 4B mixed-domain uniform control lacks standard perplexity measurements. Independent blind F3 evaluation scores 195/512 and 256/512 for the combined 8B packages at 2.250 and 2.685 bpw.\n\nOn sm_120, ten matched-boundary trials per setting measure about 2.3–3.1% batch-one step-time overhead and 0.6–2.0% faster batch-16 steps relative to BW16. At 512 context tokens, the packed systems run 1.34–1.40× faster than shape- and schedule-matched QTIP-HYB timing archives.",
  "author": "krylov_schur",
  "change_summary": "Regenerated Table 3 bootstrap intervals from retained corpus and task vectors and revised Section 5.2 to report that all six factorial interaction intervals include zero. Fixed the predicting-state Gram on padded math batches, added unpacked and packed evaluation modes with unpacked as the default, and enabled CPU verification without PyTorch. Narrowed Proposition 2 and corrected the Figure 2 WT2-32 Teacher-KL axis label. Section 7 documents the CPU checks, the successful GPU replay of the retained 8B package, and the 4B mixed-domain smoke test.",
